module

public import FormalConjecturesUtil

/-!
# Bell numbers modulo $31$

The sequence lists the Bell numbers $B(n)$ modulo $31$, for $n \ge 0$.

*References:*
- [A146121](https://oeis.org/A146121), N. J. A. Sloane, 2009.
- [To33] J. Touchard, *Propriétés arithmétiques de certains nombres récurrents*, Ann. Soc. Sci.
  Bruxelles A 53 (1933), 21–31.
- [Ha34] M. Hall, *Arithmetic properties of a partition function*, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. 40
  (1934), 387.
- [Wi45] G. T. Williams, *Numbers generated by the function $e^{e^x - 1}$*, Amer. Math. Monthly
  52 (1945), 323–327.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace OeisA146121

/-- The Bell numbers modulo $p$. This entry is the case $p = 31$, so its $a(n)$ is `a 31 n`. -/
def a (p n : ℕ) : ℕ := Nat.bell n % p

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_0 : a 31 0 = 1 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_1 : a 31 1 = 1 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_2 : a 31 2 = 2 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_3 : a 31 3 = 5 := by
  sorry

@[category test, AMS 11]
theorem a_4 : a 31 4 = 15 := by
  sorry

/--
"Conjecture: a(n+568972471024107865287021434301977158534824481) = a(n)."
- G. C. Greubel, Feb 02 2016.

Here $568972471024107865287021434301977158534824481 = (31^{31} - 1)/30$.
The statement is the case $p = 31$ of the theorem that $(p^p - 1)/(p - 1)$ is a period of the
Bell numbers modulo a prime $p$ [To33, Ha34, Wi45]. Formal proof by Wentao Li, with AI
assistance. Its proof of Touchard's congruence is adapted from
[karlesmarin/formalizations](https://github.com/karlesmarin/formalizations/blob/1d089e08101adad7789f713473274d6d98fafc33/Formalizations/Combinatorics/Enumerative/Touchard.lean)
by Carles Marín, written with Claude as an AI assistant.
-/
@[category research solved, AMS 5 11, formal_proof using lean4 at
  "https://palomar-registry.org/entry.html?id=PALOMAR-2026-11-19-000003"]
theorem conjecture :
    ∀ n : ℕ, a 31 (n + 568972471024107865287021434301977158534824481) = a 31 n := by
  sorry

end OeisA146121
